{
  "id": "L14-balanced-votes",
  "level": 14,
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "use": "test",
  "status": "ready",
  "title": "Balanced Votes",
  "statement": "A poll records each vote in order as 1 (yes) or 0 (no). Return the length of the longest stretch of consecutive votes with as many yes votes as no votes, or 0 if there is none.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "votes = [0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0]",
      "output": "4"
    },
    {
      "input": "votes = [1, 1, 1]",
      "output": "0"
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= votes.length <= 100000",
    "votes[i] is 0 or 1"
  ],
  "answerKey": {
    "pattern": "Prefix sums with the first index of each total",
    "keyPoints": [
      "Count a no vote as −1 and a yes vote as +1",
      "A balanced stretch is one where two running totals are equal",
      "Store the first index where each total appears (total 0 at index −1)",
      "The longest stretch is the largest distance between equal totals"
    ],
    "timeComplexity": "O(n)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(n)",
    "edgeCases": [
      "No balanced stretch",
      "The whole poll is balanced",
      "Alternating votes"
    ],
    "acceptableSlowerApproaches": [
      "Check every stretch with a running count: O(n²)"
    ]
  },
  "hints": [
    "Turn the problem into a sum: what if a no vote counts as −1?",
    "A balanced stretch then sums to 0, so its two ends have equal running totals.",
    "Remember the first index of each running total; the answer is the largest i − first[total]."
  ],
  "starterCode": {
    "javascript": "function longestBalanced(votes) {\n  // return the longest balanced length\n}",
    "java": "class Solution {\n  int longestBalanced(int[] votes) {\n    // return the longest balanced length\n  }\n}"
  },
